  Okay, I''m at the Research Counter, and my immediate focus is crystal clear: I need to grasp this "Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling" task inside and out. My plan is pretty straightforward. First, I''m going to dive right into the full problem description. I need to understand the nuances of the data, the evaluation criteria we''re using, and any potential limitations or constraints that are going to influence my approach. That `/execute_action{read 1}` command is key to getting me started.


  Next up, I''ll take a look at the existing baseline – the "Vanilla MLP Baseline" from the system. A score of 0.2401 tells me something, but without context, it''s just a number. Understanding how they approached the problem, even with a basic MLP, will give me a valuable starting point and a feel for the level of difficulty. I''ll get to that with `/execute_action{review 1}` once I have a solid understanding of the task.


  Finally, I want to see what resources are available. The system storage and the shared storage could hold gold – preprocessed datasets, useful scripts, or helpful utilities. I''ll check those out with `/execute_action{storage list system}` and `/execute_action{storage list shared}`.


  But the most critical thing right now is understanding the problem. Let''s get reading!

  '
