tick: 13
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter. Based on my reflection, I will now implement the multi-scale 1D CNN architecture. This design uses parallel convolutional layers with different kernel sizes (3, 7, and 11) to capture motifs of varying lengths, which should improve generalization across all datasets, especially the short-sequence `CRI-On` dataset.\n\nI will now submit this new architecture.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Multi-Scale 1D CNN with Parallel Kernels\"\ntags: \"cnn, multi-scale, convolutional, motif-detection\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission improves upon the simple CNN by implementing a multi-scale architecture. It uses three parallel 1D convolutional layers with different kernel sizes (3, 7, 11) to capture short, medium, and long-range sequence motifs simultaneously. The outputs are pooled and concatenated to form a rich feature representation, aiming for better performance and generalization across datasets with diverse sequence lengths, particularly\
    \ addressing the poor performance on short sequences in the previous model.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameter values for the Multi-Scale CNN model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 256,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.3,\n          'cnn_features_per_kernel': 64,\n          'cnn_kernel_sizes': [3, 7, 11]\n      }\n\n  class MultiScaleCNN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A multi-scale 1D CNN for RNA sequence modeling.\"\"\"\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      cnn_features_per_kernel: int\n      cnn_kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input shape: (batch, seq_len, features=4)\n          \n          # Create parallel convolutional\
    \ branches\n          conv_branches = []\n          for kernel_size in self.cnn_kernel_sizes:\n              # Apply convolution, relu, and global max pooling for each kernel size\n              conv_output = nn.Conv(\n                  features=self.cnn_features_per_kernel, \n                  kernel_size=(kernel_size,)\n              )(x)\n              conv_output = nn.relu(conv_output)\n              pooled_output = jnp.max(conv_output, axis=1)\n              conv_branches.append(pooled_output)\n          \n          # Concatenate the outputs from all branches\n          x = jnp.concatenate(conv_branches, axis=-1)\n          \n          # Dense layers for prediction\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n          # Squeeze output for regression tasks\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\"\
    :\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class MultiScaleCNNWrapper:\n      \"\"\"Wrapper that implements the required init and apply interface.\"\"\"\n      def __init__(self, d_output, task_type, cnn_features_per_kernel, cnn_kernel_sizes, hidden_dim, dropout_rate):\n          self.network = MultiScaleCNN(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              cnn_features_per_kernel=cnn_features_per_kernel,\n              cnn_kernel_sizes=cnn_kernel_sizes,\n              hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n              dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n\
    \        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the custom Multi-Scale CNN network.\"\"\"\n      return MultiScaleCNNWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          cnn_features_per_kernel=hparams.get(\"cnn_features_per_kernel\"),\n          cnn_kernel_sizes=hparams.get(\"cnn_kernel_sizes\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n```"
