parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 19\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent pursuing scientific knowledge through structured experimentation and collaborative inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 54,574 / 300,000 used (18%)\n- Agent Age: 19 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Hybrid Multi-Scale CNN-GRU for Sequential Motif Modeling' (ID: 28) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.4781117075403837\n**APA_R2:** 0.8598\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0832\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9436\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4973\n**PRS_R2:** -0.0000\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8860\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.0769\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 28\n\n## Summary\n\
    **SUCCESS** - The submission has been fixed and is now running without crashes. The code successfully passed the initialization phase and is executing the training loop.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (v1) had two critical errors related to the GRU (Gated Recurrent Unit) layer implementation:\n\n1. **Missing required parameter**: Line 20 created `gru_cell = nn.GRUCell()` without the required `features` argument. The Flax GRUCell requires specifying the hidden size via the `features` parameter.\n\n2. **Incorrect scan implementation**: The code attempted to manually implement a scan loop using `jax.lax.scan` with custom carry/state management, but had shape mismatches. The scan function was returning carries with incompatible shapes (expected `[hidden_size]` but got `[batch_size, hidden_size]`).\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (Failed)\n- Added the missing `features=self.gru_hidden_size` parameter to `nn.GRUCell()`\n- Attempted to fix the scan loop manually with proper state\
    \ initialization\n- **Result**: Still failed due to shape mismatch in the scan function's carry state\n\n### Version 3 (SUCCESS)\n- Replaced the manual GRU cell + scan implementation with Flax's built-in `nn.RNN` wrapper\n- Changed from:\n  ```python\n  gru_cell = nn.GRUCell()\n  hidden = gru_cell.initialize_carry(...)\n  hidden, _ = nn.scan(...)(hidden, x)\n  ```\n- To:\n  ```python\n  gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size))\n  x = gru(x)\n  x = x[:, -1, :]  # Take the final hidden state\n  ```\n\n### Key Changes in submission_v3.py:\n1. Line 45: Used `nn.RNN` wrapper which correctly handles the scan loop internally\n2. Line 48: Properly extracted the final timestep output using `x[:, -1, :]`\n3. Eliminated manual carry state management and shape handling issues\n\n## Technical Details\nThe `nn.RNN` module in Flax automatically handles:\n- Proper initialization of hidden states\n- Correct scanning over the sequence dimension\n- Shape management for batch processing\n\
    - Return of all timestep outputs (from which we extract the final state)\n\nThis is the recommended approach in Flax for applying recurrent layers, as it handles all the edge cases and shape transformations correctly.\n\n## Result\nThe code now successfully:\n- ✅ Passes network initialization\n- ✅ Runs forward passes without crashes\n- ✅ Executes the training loop\n- ✅ Integrates properly with the multi-scale CNN architecture\n\nThe evaluation is running normally and will complete when the training finishes or reaches the configured time limit.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 256,\n     \
    \   'dropout_rate': 0.4,\n        'cnn_features_per_kernel': 48,\n        'cnn_kernel_sizes': [3, 7, 11],\n        'gru_hidden_size': 128\n    }\n\nclass MultiScaleCNNGRU(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    cnn_features_per_kernel: int\n    cnn_kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]\n    gru_hidden_size: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # 1. Multi-scale convolutions\n        conv_outputs = []\n        for kernel_size in self.cnn_kernel_sizes:\n            conv_out = nn.Conv(\n                features=self.cnn_features_per_kernel,\n                kernel_size=(kernel_size,),\n                padding='SAME'\n            )(x)\n            conv_outputs.append(conv_out)\n\n        # 2. Concatenate feature maps\n        x = jnp.concatenate(conv_outputs, axis=-1)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n\n        # 3. GRU layer to model dependencies between motifs\n        # Use RNN module which handles the\
    \ scan loop internally\n        gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size))\n\n        # Apply GRU to the sequence (expects [batch, seq_len, features])\n        x = gru(x)\n\n        # 4. Use the final hidden state as the sequence representation\n        # Take the last timestep output\n        x = x[:, -1, :]\n\n        # 5. Prediction Head\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return x.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            return x\n\nclass CNNGRUWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, d_output, task_type, cnn_features_per_kernel, cnn_kernel_sizes, gru_hidden_size, hidden_dim, dropout_rate):\n        self.network = MultiScaleCNNGRU(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            cnn_features_per_kernel=cnn_features_per_kernel,\n\
    \            cnn_kernel_sizes=cnn_kernel_sizes,\n            gru_hidden_size=gru_hidden_size,\n            hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n            dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n      if deterministic:\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n      else:\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return CNNGRUWrapper(\n        d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n        task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n\
    \        cnn_features_per_kernel=hparams.get(\"cnn_features_per_kernel\"),\n        cnn_kernel_sizes=hparams.get(\"cnn_kernel_sizes\"),\n        gru_hidden_size=hparams.get(\"gru_hidden_size\"),\n        hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif\
    \ optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 768 CPUs, 64 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network:\
