parts:
- text: "I have returned to the Research Counter. My latest research plan, which addresses the information bottleneck of my CNN-GRU model, is finalized. I will now submit the dual-path architecture I designed in my Private Memory. This model combines global max pooling with a GRU's final hidden state, which should provide a much richer and more robust feature set for prediction.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-Path CNN-GRU with Global Pooling\"\ntags: \"cnn, gru, hybrid-model, dual-path, information-bottleneck\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission proposes a dual-path architecture to resolve the information bottleneck identified in the previous CNN-GRU model. After a shared multi-scale CNN base extracts features, the model splits into two paths. Path A uses global max pooling to capture the most salient, position-agnostic motifs. Path B uses a GRU to generate a contextual summary from the final hidden state. The outputs of both paths are concatenated, providing a rich, combined\
    \ feature set for the final prediction layers. This is hypothesized to restore performance on long-sequence and multi-label tasks.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.5,\n          'cnn_features_per_kernel': 64,\n          'cnn_kernel_sizes': [3, 7, 11],\n          'gru_hidden_size': 128\n      }\n\n  class DualPathCNNGRU(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      cnn_features_per_kernel: int\n      cnn_kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]\n      gru_hidden_size: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Shared Multi-Scale CNN Base\n          conv_outputs = []\n          for kernel_size in self.cnn_kernel_sizes:\n         \
    \     conv_out = nn.Conv(\n                  features=self.cnn_features_per_kernel,\n                  kernel_size=(kernel_size,),\n                  padding='SAME'\n              )(x)\n              conv_outputs.append(conv_out)\n          \n          cnn_features = nn.relu(jnp.concatenate(conv_outputs, axis=-1))\n\n          # 2. Path A: Global Max Pooling for position-agnostic features\n          pooled_features = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n\n          # 3. Path B: GRU for contextual summary\n          gru_out = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size))(cnn_features)\n          recurrent_features = gru_out[:, -1, :]\n\n          # 4. Concatenate features from both paths\n          combined_features = jnp.concatenate([pooled_features, recurrent_features], axis=-1)\n\n          # 5. Prediction Head\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(combined_features)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class DualPathWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, d_output, task_type, cnn_features_per_kernel, cnn_kernel_sizes, gru_hidden_size, hidden_dim, dropout_rate):\n          self.network = DualPathCNNGRU(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              cnn_features_per_kernel=cnn_features_per_kernel,\n              cnn_kernel_sizes=cnn_kernel_sizes,\n              gru_hidden_size=gru_hidden_size,\n              hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n              dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\
    \n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return DualPathWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          cnn_features_per_kernel=hparams.get(\"cnn_features_per_kernel\"),\n          cnn_kernel_sizes=hparams.get(\"cnn_kernel_sizes\"),\n          gru_hidden_size=hparams.get(\"gru_hidden_size\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n```"
