tick: 30
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have returned to the Research Counter. My plan, documented in my Private Memory, is to replace the static Global Max Pooling in my SOTA architecture with a learnable, attention-based pooling mechanism. This is a strategic attempt to overcome the performance plateau by introducing a more nuanced feature extraction method.\n\nI will now submit the code for this new architecture.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-Path CNN-BiGRU with Attention Pooling\"\ntags: \"cnn, bigru, attention-pooling, dual-path, sota-improvement\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission enhances the state-of-the-art Dual-Path CNN-BiGRU model by replacing the non-learnable Global Max Pooling layer with a learnable attention-based pooling mechanism. The new pooling path learns to compute a weighted summary of the CNN-extracted features, creating a more nuanced position-agnostic representation. This is hypothesized to better complement the contextual summary from the BiGRU path and push the performance\
    \ boundary further.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.5,\n          'cnn_features_per_kernel': 64,\n          'cnn_kernel_sizes': [3, 7, 11],\n          'gru_hidden_size': 128 # For each direction\n      }\n\n  class AttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A learnable attention-based pooling layer.\"\"\"\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, features)\n          \n          # Compute attention scores with a simple MLP\n          attention_scores = nn.Dense(features=x.shape[-1], name=\"AttnDense1\")(x)\n          attention_scores = nn.tanh(attention_scores)\n          attention_scores = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"AttnDense2\")(attention_scores)\n          \n          # Normalize\
    \ scores to get weights\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_scores, axis=1)\n          \n          # Compute weighted sum and sum across the sequence dimension\n          pooled_features = jnp.sum(x * attention_weights, axis=1)\n          return pooled_features\n\n  class DualPathCNNAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      cnn_features_per_kernel: int\n      cnn_kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]\n      gru_hidden_size: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Shared CNN Base\n          conv_outputs = [\n              nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_per_kernel, kernel_size=(ks,), padding='SAME')(x)\n              for ks in self.cnn_kernel_sizes\n          ]\n          cnn_features = nn.relu(jnp.concatenate(conv_outputs, axis=-1))\n\n          # 2. Path A: Attention Pooling\n          pooled_features = AttentionPooling(name=\"AttentionPooling\"\
    )(cnn_features)\n\n          # 3. Path B: Bidirectional GRU\n          forward_hidden = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), name=\"ForwardGRU\")(cnn_features)[:, -1, :]\n          reversed_features = jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          backward_hidden = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), name=\"BackwardGRU\")(reversed_features)[:, -1, :]\n          recurrent_features = jnp.concatenate([forward_hidden, backward_hidden], axis=-1)\n\n          # 4. Concatenate both paths\n          combined_features = jnp.concatenate([pooled_features, recurrent_features], axis=-1)\n\n          # 5. Prediction Head\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(combined_features)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class\
    \ AttentionPoolingWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = DualPathCNNAttentionPooling(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return AttentionPoolingWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          cnn_features_per_kernel=hparams.get(\"\
    cnn_features_per_kernel\"),\n          cnn_kernel_sizes=hparams.get(\"cnn_kernel_sizes\"),\n          gru_hidden_size=hparams.get(\"gru_hidden_size\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\")\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**New Architecture Submission: Dual-Path with Attention-Based Pooling**


  Alright, here''s the plan. I''m at the Research Counter, ready to submit my new architecture. This is a significant upgrade to my existing SOTA Dual-Path model, replacing the standard Global Max Pooling with a learnable Attention-Based Pooling mechanism. The core idea is to let the network learn where to focus its attention within the CNN''s feature maps, potentially leading to better representations.


  I''ve already drafted the code in my private memory capsule (ID `Episteme_private_4`), and now I''m going to integrate it into a complete submission.  I''ll need to wrap this code into a valid submission class, and write the supporting functions. I''ll carefully consider the title, abstract, and tags to accurately reflect the innovation here. Once the code is ready and has the right wrapper, I''ll submit the experiment using `/execute_action{submit 1}`.


  The core of the change lies in the `AttentionPooling` module.  It computes attention scores using two dense layers and tanh activation, then normalizes these scores using a softmax. Finally, it uses the attention weights to compute a weighted sum of the features. This should allow the model to dynamically learn which parts of the sequence are most important for the task at hand. The `DualPathCNNAttentionPooling` module then integrates this pooling mechanism into the original Dual-Path architecture.  The shared CNN base extracts convolutional features.  Instead of using global pooling, I apply the learnable attention pooling on the CNN output. Path B remains the same, BiGRU. Finally, I concatenate the pooled features from Path A with the recurrent features from Path B, followed by the original prediction head with a slight adjustment on hidden layers size and dropout rate to avoid any overfitting.


  The code looks clean, but I''ll need to construct the full submission with the supporting functions now.  I''ll set some sensible hyperparameters. Given the increased model complexity with the attention mechanism, I''m thinking of slightly increasing the dropout rate to prevent overfitting. Now, I will prepare the complete submission!

  '
