tick: 35
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter to begin my planned ablation study. I will now submit the first experiment: the dual-path architecture with the recurrent (BiGRU) path removed. This will isolate and quantify the performance of the Multi-Scale CNN with Global Max Pooling, using the same hyperparameters as my SOTA model for a fair comparison.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation: Multi-Scale CNN with Global Pooling Only\"\ntags: \"ablation-study, cnn, pooling, publication-prep\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the first ablation experiment on the Dual-Path CNN-BiGRU model (ID 49). This submission completely removes the Bidirectional GRU path, leaving only the Multi-Scale CNN feature extractor followed by a Global Max Pooling layer. The purpose is to quantify the performance contribution of the position-agnostic pooling path in isolation, using identical hyperparameters to the full model for a controlled comparison.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from\
    \ jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using the same HPs as the full model (ID 49) for a fair ablation.\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.5,\n          'cnn_features_per_kernel': 64,\n          'cnn_kernel_sizes': [3, 7, 11],\n          'gru_hidden_size': 128 # Kept for signature consistency, but unused.\n      }\n\n  class AblationPoolingOnly(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      cnn_features_per_kernel: int\n      cnn_kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Multi-Scale CNN Base\n          conv_outputs = []\n          for kernel_size in self.cnn_kernel_sizes:\n              conv_out = nn.Conv(\n                  features=self.cnn_features_per_kernel,\n               \
    \   kernel_size=(kernel_size,),\n                  padding='SAME'\n              )(x)\n              conv_outputs.append(conv_out)\n          \n          cnn_features = nn.relu(jnp.concatenate(conv_outputs, axis=-1))\n\n          # 2. Global Max Pooling Path (Recurrent path is removed)\n          pooled_features = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n\n          # 3. Prediction Head\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(pooled_features)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class AblationWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          # We don't need gru_hidden_size for this ablation model\n          kwargs.pop('gru_hidden_size', None)\n          self.network = AblationPoolingOnly(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key,\
    \ dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return AblationWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n          cnn_features_per_kernel=hparams.get(\"cnn_features_per_kernel\"),\n          cnn_kernel_sizes=hparams.get(\"cnn_kernel_sizes\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"\
    ),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"),\n          gru_hidden_size=hparams.get(\"gru_hidden_size\") # Pass for consistent signature\n      )\n```"
