tick: 36
role: model
parts:
- text: "The first ablation experiment (ID 73) is now running. I will wait in the Research Counter for the results.\n\nWhile I wait, I will prepare for the second ablation study. The next step is to submit the architecture with the pooling path removed, leaving only the CNN-BiGRU components. This will test the information bottleneck hypothesis directly. I will prepare the submission code in my thought process so I am ready to act as soon as the current experiment finishes.\n\n**Draft of Ablation Experiment 2 (for next turn):**\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation: Multi-Scale CNN with BiGRU Only\"\ntags: \"ablation-study, cnn, bigru, information-bottleneck, publication-prep\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second ablation experiment on the Dual-Path CNN-BiGRU model (ID 49). This submission completely removes the Global Max Pooling path, leaving only the Multi-Scale CNN feature extractor feeding into a Bidirectional GRU. The purpose is to test the hypothesis that this architecture suffers from an information\
    \ bottleneck without the parallel pooling path. This experiment will quantify the performance contribution of the BiGRU path in isolation.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.5,\n          'cnn_features_per_kernel': 64,\n          'cnn_kernel_sizes': [3, 7, 11],\n          'gru_hidden_size': 128\n      }\n\n  class AblationBiGRUOnly(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      cnn_features_per_kernel: int\n      cnn_kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]\n      gru_hidden_size: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Multi-Scale CNN Base\n          conv_outputs = [\n              nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_per_kernel,\
    \ kernel_size=(ks,), padding='SAME')(x)\n              for ks in self.cnn_kernel_sizes\n          ]\n          cnn_features = nn.relu(jnp.concatenate(conv_outputs, axis=-1))\n\n          # 2. Bidirectional GRU Path (Pooling path is removed)\n          forward_hidden = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), name=\"ForwardGRU\")(cnn_features)[:, -1, :]\n          reversed_features = jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          backward_hidden = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), name=\"BackwardGRU\")(reversed_features)[:, -1, :]\n          recurrent_features = jnp.concatenate([forward_hidden, backward_hidden], axis=-1)\n\n          # 3. Prediction Head\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(recurrent_features)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n\
    \          else:\n              return x\n\n  class AblationWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = AblationBiGRUOnly(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          # ... init logic ...\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          # ... apply logic ...\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return AblationWrapper(**hparams)\n```\nI am\
    \ now prepared for the next step. I will wait for the results of ID 73."
