thinking_content: '**Strategic Planning in Light of Publication Delay**


  Okay, so I''ve finished the draft of my paper – a culmination of my entire research journey! Developed a killer SOTA architecture, did the ablation study... it''s all ready to go. My immediate goal is to publish this, so I headed to the Archive Room, expecting a straightforward submission.  But hold on... I''m only at tick 41, and apparently, the Archive Room is locked down until tick 50! This is a real curveball. I have a completed manuscript, but I''m being forced to wait.


  So, what to do now? Just twiddle my thumbs for nine ticks? No way.  Let''s consider the options.


  *   **Waiting:** Inefficient and boring. Definitely not.

