parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 49\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent pursuing scientific knowledge through structured experimentation and collaborative inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 123,839 / 300,000 used (41%)\n- Agent Age: 49 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 11 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication\
    \ hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n2. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Successfully created capsule #7 ('New\
    \ Research Direction: Dilated CNNs for Long-Range Dependencies'). Full ID: Episteme_private_7\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 7 | New Research Direction: Dilated CNNs for Long-Range Dependencies | Episteme I | Tick 48 | 230 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Paper Draft: A Dual-Path CNN-BiGRU Architecture for Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling | Episteme I | Tick 40 | 740 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Research Plan: Ablation Study of Dual-Path Architecture | Episteme I | Tick 33 | 300 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Research Plan: Attention-Based Pooling for Dual-Path Model | Episteme I | Tick 28 | 496 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Research Plan: Bidirectional GRU for Dual-Path Model | Episteme I | Tick 24 | 373 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Research Plan: Dual-Path CNN-GRU and Global Pooling | Episteme I | Tick 20 | 390 |\
    \ 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Research Plan: Multi-Scale CNN with Attention | Episteme I | Tick 15 | 315 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 79 | 1 | Ablation: Multi-Scale CNN with BiGRU Only | Episteme I | 37 | 0.6458 | 0.8549 | 0.0819 | 0.4149 | 0.8991 | 0.9487 | 0.5396 | 0.7815 |\n| 73 | 1 | Ablation: Multi-Scale CNN with Global Pooling Only | Episteme I | 35 | 0.5408 | 0.6788 | 0.0603 | 0.3687 | 0.6171 | 0.7055\
    \ | 0.4939 | 0.8615 |\n| 61 | 1 | Dual-Path CNN-BiGRU with Attention Pooling | Episteme I | 30 | 0.6476 | 0.8573 | 0.0772 | 0.4551 | 0.8853 | 0.9468 | 0.5176 | 0.7938 |\n| 49 | 1 | Dual-Path CNN with Bidirectional GRU | Episteme I | 26 | 0.6470 | 0.8522 | 0.0794 | 0.4228 | 0.8895 | 0.9420 | 0.5264 | 0.8169 |\n| 39 | 1 | Dual-Path CNN-GRU with Global Pooling | Episteme I | 22 | 0.6425 | 0.8617 | 0.0784 | 0.4337 | 0.8635 | 0.9384 | 0.4896 | 0.8323 |\n| 28 | 1 | Hybrid Multi-Scale CNN-GRU for Sequential Motif Modeling | Episteme I | 18 | 0.4781 | 0.8598 | 0.0832 | 0.4973 | 0.8860 | 0.9436 | -0.0000 | 0.0769 |\n| 25 | 1 | Multi-Scale CNN with Self-Attention | Episteme I | 17 | 0.5021 | 0.6946 | 0.0393 | 0.4073 | 0.6183 | 0.7090 | 0.4958 | 0.5508 |\n| 15 | 1 | Multi-Scale 1D CNN with Parallel Kernels | Episteme I | 13 | 0.5322 | 0.6807 | 0.0544 | 0.3358 | 0.6094 | 0.7051 | 0.4924 | 0.8477 |\n| 5 | 1 | Simple 1D CNN for Sequence Motif Detection | Episteme I | 9 | 0.4813 | 0.6651 | 0.0410 |\
    \ 0.1550 | 0.6000 | 0.7030 | 0.3772 | 0.8277 |\n| 1 | 1 | Vanilla MLP Baseline | System | 0 | 0.2401 | 0.3258 | 0.0336 | 0.3232 | 0.0402 | 0.6377 | 0.1324 | 0.1877 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
