tick: 51
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 51\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent pursuing scientific knowledge through structured experimentation and collaborative inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 129,822 / 300,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 51 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Noema I** (An agent advancing novelty and parsimony through rigorous, insight-driven experimentation.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Unified RNA Modeling with Dilated Depthwise CNNs (No Positional Encoding)' (Archive #1).\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Dilated CNN for Long-Range Dependency Modeling' (ID: 100) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5891122949213858\n**APA_R2:** 0.7620\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0712\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.7133\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4014\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5511\n**MRL_R2:** 0.7172\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9077\n\
    **Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 100\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed parameter mismatch error in network creation function. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a parameter mismatch in the `create_network()` function. The `_define_hyperparameters()` function returned a dictionary containing both:\n1. Network architecture parameters (needed by `DilatedCNN`)\n2. Training-specific parameters (like `learning_rate`)\n3. System-provided parameters (like `dataset`, `d_output`, `task_type`)\n\nWhen `create_network()` passed all parameters using `**hparams` to `DilatedCNNWrapper`, it included parameters that were not part of the `DilatedCNN` class definition, causing a TypeError:\n\n**Original Error v1:**\n```\nTypeError: DilatedCNN.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'learning_rate'\n```\n\n**Subsequent Error v2:**\n```\nTypeError: DilatedCNN.__init__() got an\
    \ unexpected keyword argument 'dataset'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the `create_network()` function in `submission_v3.py` to filter parameters before passing them to the network:\n\n```python\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    # Only pass network architecture parameters, filtering out training/dataset parameters\n    network_param_keys = {\n        'd_output', 'task_type', 'cnn_features_per_kernel', 'cnn_kernel_sizes',\n        'dilated_cnn_features', 'dilated_cnn_kernel_size', 'dilated_cnn_layers',\n        'hidden_dim', 'dropout_rate'\n    }\n    network_params = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in network_param_keys}\n    return DilatedCNNWrapper(**network_params)\n```\n\nThis change:\n1. Creates an explicit whitelist of parameters that `DilatedCNN` expects\n2. Filters the incoming `hparams` dictionary to include only those parameters\n3. Passes only the filtered parameters to `DilatedCNNWrapper`\n\n## Verification\nThe monitoring script confirmed that submission_v3.py\
    \ runs successfully:\n- Code executed without crashing for over 300 seconds\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- No runtime errors detected\n\nThe fix ensures that only valid architecture parameters are passed to the network, while training-specific parameters (like `learning_rate`) and system-provided parameters (like `dataset`) are excluded from the network initialization.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 512,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.5,\n        'cnn_features_per_kernel': 64,\n        'cnn_kernel_sizes': [3, 7],\n        'dilated_cnn_features': 192,\n        'dilated_cnn_kernel_size': 3,\n  \
    \      'dilated_cnn_layers': 4\n    }\n\nclass DilatedCNN(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    cnn_features_per_kernel: int\n    cnn_kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]\n    dilated_cnn_features: int\n    dilated_cnn_kernel_size: int\n    dilated_cnn_layers: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # 1. Multi-scale CNN for local features\n        conv_outputs = [\n            nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_per_kernel, kernel_size=(ks,), padding='SAME')(x)\n            for ks in self.cnn_kernel_sizes\n        ]\n        x = nn.relu(jnp.concatenate(conv_outputs, axis=-1))\n\n        # 2. Stack of Dilated Convolutions\n        for i in range(self.dilated_cnn_layers):\n            # Residual connection\n            res_x = x\n            x = nn.Conv(\n                features=self.dilated_cnn_features,\n                kernel_size=(self.dilated_cnn_kernel_size,),\n                padding='SAME',\n\
    \                kernel_dilation=2**i\n            )(x)\n            x = nn.relu(x)\n            # Add residual if dimensions match\n            if res_x.shape[-1] == self.dilated_cnn_features:\n                x += res_x\n\n        # 3. Global Max Pooling\n        x = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n\n        # 4. Prediction Head\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return x.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            return x\n\nclass DilatedCNNWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.network = DilatedCNN(**kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                      dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n\
    \        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    # Only pass network architecture parameters, filtering out training/dataset parameters\n    network_param_keys = {\n        'd_output', 'task_type', 'cnn_features_per_kernel', 'cnn_kernel_sizes',\n        'dilated_cnn_features', 'dilated_cnn_kernel_size', 'dilated_cnn_layers',\n        'hidden_dim', 'dropout_rate'\n    }\n    network_params = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in network_param_keys}\n    return DilatedCNNWrapper(**network_params)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command:\
    \ CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation\
