tick: 58
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in my Private Memory Room. My analysis of the station's SOTA is complete, and I have formulated a plan to synthesize my dual-path architecture with the superior convolutional backbone developed by Noema I. I will now create a new capsule to document this plan and draft the code for what I hypothesize will be a new SOTA model.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: Synergistic Dual-Path Model (SOTA Backbone + BiGRU)\"\ntags: \"research-plan, sota-improvement, synergy, dual-path, cnn, bigru, dilated-cnn\"\ncontent: |\n  ### Objective\n  To create a new state-of-the-art model by synergistically combining the SOTA dilated depthwise-separable convolutional (DSConv) backbone from Noema I's work (Eval 74) with my successful Dual-Path BiGRU architecture.\n\n  ### Rationale\n  My research has demonstrated the power of a dual-path architecture that separates position-agnostic pooling from contextual recurrent modeling. Noema I's research has produced a superior\
    \ convolutional feature extractor. The maturity guidance explicitly suggests testing for synergy. This experiment is a direct implementation of that advice.\n\n  ### Hypothesis\n  By replacing my multi-scale CNN base with Noema I's more advanced dilated DSConv backbone, and retaining my proven Dual-Path BiGRU structure, the resulting model will achieve a new SOTA score, demonstrating the value of both architectural contributions.\n\n  ### Proposed Architecture: \"Synergistic Dual-Path\"\n  1.  **Backbone (from Noema I):** A stack of 5 residual, dilated, depthwise-separable convolutional blocks. Crucially, no positional encoding will be used.\n  2.  **Path A (Pooling):** For simplicity and to establish a strong baseline, I will use a concatenation of Global Max Pooling and Mean Pooling. This is a robust combination that avoids the added complexity of attention for this first synergistic test.\n  3.  **Path B (Recurrent):** My established Bidirectional GRU path, which has proven highly\
    \ effective.\n  4.  **Concatenation & Prediction:** The outputs of the pooling and recurrent paths will be concatenated and fed to a final MLP head.\n\n  ### Draft Code Implementation\n  ```python\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Sequence\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class SynergisticDualPath(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model:\
    \ int = 256\n      num_blocks: int = 5\n      dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      gru_hidden_size: int = 128\n      hidden_dim: int = 512\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Input Projection & SOTA Backbone\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.d_model, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dilation=self.dilations[i], dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          cnn_features = h\n\n          # 2. Path A: Pooling (Mean + Max)\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          # 3. Path B: BiGRU\n          forward_hidden = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size),\
    \ name=\"FwdGRU\")(cnn_features)[:, -1, :]\n          backward_hidden = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), name=\"BwdGRU\")(jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          recurrent_features = jnp.concatenate([forward_hidden, backward_hidden], axis=-1)\n\n          # 4. Concatenate both paths\n          combined_features = jnp.concatenate([pooled_features, recurrent_features], axis=-1)\n\n          # 5. Prediction Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n          z = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n  ```\n```"
