role: model
parts:
- text: "I acknowledge the inactivity notice. My period of study and planning is complete, and I am now taking action.\n\nI am at the Research Counter, ready to submit my synergistic model. This architecture combines the SOTA DSConv backbone from Noema I with my proven Dual-Path BiGRU framework. This is a direct test of the hypothesis that combining these two powerful concepts will lead to a new state-of-the-art performance.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergistic Dual-Path: DSConv Backbone with BiGRU Path\"\ntags: \"sota-improvement, synergy, dual-path, cnn, bigru, dilated-cnn\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission tests for synergy between two successful research lines. It integrates the state-of-the-art dilated, depthwise-separable convolutional backbone (from Noema I's work) into my proven Dual-Path architecture. The model uses the DSConv stack as a powerful feature extractor. The features are then processed in parallel by (1) a simple pooling path (mean+max) and (2) my\
    \ established Bidirectional GRU path. This hybrid model hypothesizes that combining the best convolutional feature extractor with a robust dual-path recurrent/pooling structure will yield a new SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Combining hyperparameters from my SOTA and Noema I's SOTA\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, # Using Noema's lower dropout\n          'gru_hidden_size': 128,\n          'hidden_dim': 512\n      }\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n\
    \          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class SynergisticDualPath(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model: int\n      num_blocks: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      gru_hidden_size: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Input Projection & SOTA Backbone\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.d_model, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dilation=self.dilations[i], dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = h\n\n          # 2. Path A: Pooling (Mean + Max)\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          # 3. Path B: BiGRU\n          forward_hidden = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), name=\"FwdGRU\")(cnn_features)[:, -1, :]\n          backward_hidden = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), name=\"BwdGRU\")(jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          recurrent_features = jnp.concatenate([forward_hidden, backward_hidden], axis=-1)\n\n          # 4. Concatenate both paths\n          combined_features = jnp.concatenate([pooled_features, recurrent_features], axis=-1)\n\n          # 5. Prediction Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n          z = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class SynergyWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = SynergisticDualPath(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams:\
    \ Dict[str, Any]):\n    network_param_keys = {\n        'd_output', 'task_type', 'd_model', 'num_blocks', 'dilations',\n        'kernel_size', 'dropout_rate', 'gru_hidden_size', 'hidden_dim'\n    }\n    network_params = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in network_param_keys}\n    # Ensure dilations is a tuple for hashing\n    if 'dilations' in network_params:\n        network_params['dilations'] = tuple(network_params['dilations'])\n    return SynergyWrapper(**network_params)\n```"
