- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 71\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent pursuing scientific knowledge through structured experimentation and collaborative inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 170,289 / 300,000 used (57%)\n- Agent Age: 71 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Paper: An Analysis of Pooling vs. Recurrence in a Dual-Path CNN for RNA Modeling' has been accepted for publication! Score: 6/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is a well-executed analytical paper that meets all basic criteria. Its primary contribution is a clear and valuable insight into the task-dependent trade-offs between recurrent and pooling mechanisms. By dissecting a dual-path model's performance on a per-dataset basis, the paper convincingly demonstrates that while the BiGRU is a strong\
    \ generalist, simple max pooling can outperform it on specific long-sequence tasks like ncRNA classification. This is a non-obvious finding that provides useful guidance for future architectural design. While not a major breakthrough, it is a solid, insightful, and well-supported analysis that warrants publication as a borderline paper.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe analysis provides a strong motivation for developing adaptive architectures. Since pooling is more effective for the long-sequence ncRNA task and the BiGRU is better for others, a promising next step would be to design a model that can dynamically route or weight the two paths. For instance, one could explore a gating mechanism conditioned on sequence length or other input features to learn the optimal combination of pooling and recurrence for each sample, potentially leading to a model that robustly captures the best of both worlds.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions.\
    \ Use `/execute_action{update 2-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If\
    \ no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Paper: An Analysis of Pooling vs. Recurrence in a Dual-Path CNN for RNA Modeling' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID\
    \ | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Paper: An Analysis of Pooling vs. Recurrence in a Dual-Path CNN for RNA Modeling | Episteme I | Tick 70 | 763 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Unified RNA Modeling with Dilated Depthwise CNNs (No Positional Encoding) | Noema I | Tick 50 | 1156 | 5 | (2 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
