tick: 73
role: model
parts:
- text: "I acknowledge the inactivity notice and am taking immediate action. I am at the Research Counter to submit my new experiment based on the plan documented in my Private Memory (Capsule #10).\n\nThis \"Adaptive Gated Dual-Path\" model is my next major hypothesis. It introduces a gating mechanism to dynamically balance the influence of the pooling and recurrent paths, a direct follow-up to the insights from my published paper and its review. I will now submit the code.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Adaptive Gating for Dual-Path CNN-BiGRU\"\ntags: \"adaptive-model, gating-mechanism, dual-path, cnn, bigru, sota-improvement\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission proposes a novel adaptive architecture that builds upon the dual-path framework. Following the insight that pooling and recurrent paths excel on different tasks, this model introduces a gating mechanism. The gate, implemented as a small MLP with a sigmoid activation, learns to produce a weight based on a summary of\
    \ the sequence features. This weight dynamically balances the contribution of the pooling path and the BiGRU path to the final representation. The hypothesis is that this adaptive approach will outperform static combinations and achieve a new SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'gru_hidden_size': 128,\n          'hidden_dim': 512\n      }\n\n  class DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\
    \ kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  class AdaptiveGatedDualPath(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model: int\n      num_blocks: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      gru_hidden_size: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. SOTA Backbone\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.d_model, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dilation=self.dilations[i], dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features\
    \ = h\n\n          # 2. Parallel Paths\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          forward_hidden = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), name=\"FwdGRU\")(cnn_features)[:, -1, :]\n          backward_hidden = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), name=\"BwdGRU\")(jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          recurrent_features = jnp.concatenate([forward_hidden, backward_hidden], axis=-1)\n          \n          # 3. Gating Mechanism\n          gate_input = jax.lax.stop_gradient(recurrent_features) # Use summary as gate input, stop gradient to stabilize\n          gate_val = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim, name=\"GateDense1\")(gate_input)\n          gate_val = nn.gelu(gate_val)\n          gate_val = nn.Dense(features=pooled_features.shape[-1], name=\"GateDense2\")(gate_val)\n          gate = nn.sigmoid(gate_val)\n\
    \          \n          # Ensure recurrent_features matches pooled_features dimension for gating\n          projected_recurrent = nn.Dense(features=pooled_features.shape[-1], name=\"RecurrentProjection\")(recurrent_features)\n\n          # 4. Gated Combination\n          combined_features = (gate * projected_recurrent) + ((1 - gate) * pooled_features)\n\n          # 5. Prediction Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n          z = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class GatedWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = AdaptiveGatedDualPath(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key)\n\
    \          return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    net_params = {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in AdaptiveGatedDualPath.__annotations__}\n    if 'dilations' in net_params: net_params['dilations'] = tuple(net_params['dilations'])\n    return GatedWrapper(**net_params)\n```"
